  "body": "CamCraft should support exporting a simulation movie showing how material was removed from stock.  This can be used by users to validate that the machining process makes sense.  It should be supported in headless mode so that it can be used during batch processing of a large number of machining jobs.\r\n\r\nThis pull request adds a  a pure-Rust, headless 3D material-removal simulation movie renderer to `camcraft-app` exposed consistently through the CLI (`camcraft-cli render-video`), the MCP JSON-RPC server (`render_simulation_video`), and Boa JS job scripts (`cam.call(\"render_simulation_video\", {...})`).\r\n\r\n[![Example video export](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e508d989-ce43-4d53-911a-d91e73997d2a)](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e508d989-ce43-4d53-911a-d91e73997d2a)\r\n\r\n\r\n### Design\r\n \r\n------\r\n- `crates/app/src/sim_video/` (zero new external crate dependencies):\r\n  - `math.rs`: `Vec3`, `Mat3` (`from_quat` matching `camcraft-geometry` `[x, y, z, w]` layout), shortest-arc `quat_slerp` with double-cover sign handling, pinhole `Camera`, slab AABB intersection, and analytic ray-cylinder / ray-cone / ray-sphere intersections for tool rendering.\r\n  - `voxel.rs`: persistent single-byte 3D voxel billet (`VoxelStock`) held in document/part frame with per-surface operation color tags (`TAG_*`), fast column-bound carving along `±Z` (`col_max_z`/`col_min_z`), general arbitrary-axis carving (`carve_oriented`) for side-on and tilted 5-axis moves, `mask_cylinder_z`, watertight `mask_mesh` ray-parity masking, 3x3x3 occupancy gradient normals, and neighborhood ambient occlusion.\r\n  - `plan.rs`: extracts generated setups, `setup_align::stored` inverse rigid alignments, WCS labels (`G54`..`G59`/`G54.1P*`) and origins, `StockShape::{Box, Cylinder, FromModel}`, tool shapes (`Flat`, `Ball`, `Bull`, `Drill`, `Chamfer`), chord-tessellated `Move::segments3` arcs, optional 5-axis tilted `Move.axis`, and part mesh volume across aligned setups.\r\n  - `render.rs`: `rayon`-parallel 3D DDA ray-marcher (Amanatides-Woo) with studio floor grid & drop shadow, Blinn-Phong metallic shading, contact cutting glow, spinning fluted analytic cutters/shanks/holders, and a depth-tested live 3D toolpath ribbon trail (blue feed, amber plunge, red rapid).\r\n  - `hud.rs`: clean-room 5x7 ASCII bitmap font rendering the setup/op top bar, tool/RPM/feed badge, WCS DRO readout, volume tracker, `M0 STOP` transition banners, and segmented operation progress bar with responsive layout clamping for narrow resolutions (e.g. 640x360).\r\n  - `encode.rs`: dual frame sinks supporting pure-Rust RGB8 PNG frame sequences (`format = \"frames\"`, zero external tools required) and raw RGB24 streaming to `ffmpeg` for `.mp4` (`libx264`), `.webm` (`libvpx`), and `.gif` (two-pass palette filter).\r\n  - `mod.rs`: orchestrator with proportional `sqrt(len)` op frame budgeting, quaternion SLERP setup re-orientation animations, auto-azimuth framing for asymmetric side-turned setups (`setup_az_bias`), single-pass frame teeing for `--per-setup` split videos, silent prior-setup carry replay for `--setup <name>`, turntable showcase spin (with upright return for side-turned final setups), optional PNG keyframe capture, and explicit validation/refusal checks (resolution bounds, even dimensions for `yuv420p` mp4/webm, `fps`, `cell_mm`, 120M voxel cap).\r\n- Wiring & safety gates:\r\n  - `crates/app/src/mcp/video.rs` & `mcp/tools.rs`: registers `render_simulation_video` (schema with `additionalProperties: false`).\r\n  - `crates/app/src/mcp/live.rs`: gates `render_simulation_video` under `GateKind::FileWrite` for live GUI MCP approval parity (#1942).\r\n  - `crates/app/src/cli_video.rs` & `cli.rs`: adds `camcraft-cli render-video` to `TOP_USAGE` and `HELP_LANES` (thin wrapper generating `cam.load` / optional `cam.generate` / `cam.call(\"render_simulation_video\", ...)`).\r\n  - Regenerated `docs/agents/mcp-tools.md` (`117 -> 118` tools) and updated `site/content/guide/automate/mcp.md`.\r\n\r\nTesting\r\n-------\r\n- New internal unit test suite `crates/app/src/sim_video/tests.rs` (16 tests):\r\n  New integration test suite `crates/app/tests/sim_video.rs` (8 hermetic tests using pure-Rust `format = \"frames\"`, zero `ffmpeg` required):\r\n  - Single-setup render + `cam.call` JS bridge & PNG header verification.\r\n  - 3-setup upright (`G54`) / 180° flip / -90° side-on render via MCP `tools/call`, checking monotonic volume reduction, part mesh volume across aligned setups, `--per-setup` directory PNG counts matching report, keyframes, and `--setup` filter silent carry parity.\r\n- Rendered real outputs end-to-end with release `camcraft-cli render-video`:\r\n  - 3-setup double-ear clevis bracket (`960x540`, `30 fps`, `0.25 mm` voxel pitch, `424x288x288` grid, `--per-setup`): 1,221 frames + 3 split MP4s + 20 PNG keyframes in 24.9s (`549.5 -> 133.7 cm^3` vs `129.5 cm^3` CAD).\r\n  - `examples/first-part.camproj` (`--generate`, `.webm` & `640x360` PNG frames): `120.0 -> 67.95 cm^3` vs `67.36 cm^3` CAD.",
